hadiths[128]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7072","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Abi Thawr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, who said: I asked for permission On the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I entered upon him to drink, and he was lying on a piece of cloth, and some of him was on the dirt and under his head. A pillow stuffed with fiber, and on top of Ahab’s head there was a stick of mud, and on the side of the drinking bowl there was a ball of pearls, so I greeted him on it, then I sat down and said: O Messenger By God, you are God’s prophet, His chosen one, and the best of His creation, and Chosroes and Caesar were on beds of gold, silk furnishings, and brocade. He said: “O Umar, these are the people whose good deeds have been hastened and are about to be cut off, and we are a people whose good deeds have been delayed for us in “Our Hereafter” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7072 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7073","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us about a crescent moon. Al-Wazzan, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He ate well and worked according to the Sunnah, and the people were safe from his evil deeds, and he will enter Paradise.” They said: “O Messenger of God, there is much of this among your nation today.” He said: “And it will happen in “For centuries after me” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7073 - True"
"7074","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told me, Al-Amash told me, Thabit bin Ubaid told me, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad told me, he said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit some of his wives. And she has a lump of honey, so he licks some of it and sits by it. So they liked that, so Aisha said to Hafsa and some of the husbands The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we said to him: We only smell the fragrance of the Maghafir from you. He said: “It is honey that I licked at so-and-so and I will not return it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7074 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7075","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Muharram told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Salih Al-Wazzan told us, Abu Al-Numan Muhammad bin Al-Fadl, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Thabit reported, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Umm Sulaim had a cup, and I did not miss any of the drink except that I made the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drink in it the honey, milk, wine, and water.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7075 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7076","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Bastam bin Muslim told us, he said: I heard Muawiyah bin Qurrah say: My father said: “We fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had no food except lions.” He said: “Do you know what the two lions are?” He said: No. He said: “Water and dates.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7076 - True"
"7077","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “If it was to attack the family of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him A month and a half, and no fire was kindled in their houses for a lamp or anything else. I said to her: What was your livelihood? She said: “Dates and water.” This is a hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7077 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7078","Ahmad ibn Ahmad al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani’ told us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf Al-Azraq, narrated by Mas’ar, on the authority of Hilal Al-Wazzan, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “What Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ate.” “And he greeted two meals on the day, except one of them dates.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7078 - True"
"7079","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Ala told us, Saeed informed us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, said: I stayed close to Abu Hurairah for two years, and he said: “O Ibn Shaqiq, do you see this stone for the stone of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? Peace and blessings of God be upon him. I saw us at that time, and no one had enough food to fill his stomach, to the point that one of us would take a stone and hold it tightly against his soles. With a rope or with a piece of cutting, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you saw me and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, distributed dates between us, and each one of them received it. From among us were seven dates, and seven of them had a glans in them, so what pleases me is a good date with it.” He said: I said: Why, Abu Hurairah? He said: “Because it made me uncomfortable, so I started to chew it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7079 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7080","Ali bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Humaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “For forty nights would come upon us and nothing would be lit in the house of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Misbah and no one else. He said: We said: That is, mother, so what did you live on? She said: “With the two lions, dates and water.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7080 - True"
"7081","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Al-Khasib bin Nasih told us, Talha bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to call dates and milk good.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7081 - Talha bin Zaid is weak"
"7082","Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Malik bin Ismail told us, Qais bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Abu Hisham Al-Rummani told us, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Salman, He said: I read in the Torah: Ablution before food is the blessing of food, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Ablution before food And after food, the blessing of food.” Qays ibn al-Rabi’ was the only one with it, on the authority of Abu Hashim, and his being alone at the height of his place is too much for it to be left in This book"
"7083","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Salama, he said: I entered upon Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, me and two men, one man. I think there was a man from us and a man from Banu Asad, so he sent them back and said: You are both sick, so treat your religion. Then he entered the exit and then left. So he took a handful of water and wiped himself with it, then he came and recited the Qur’an. We saw that we denied that, and Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “He was the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would come to the toilet and relieve himself, then he would go out and eat bread and meat with us, and he would recite the Qur’an without blocking it. And he may have said: And nothing will prevent him from reading the Qur’an except impurity - or nothing but impurity - “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7083 - True"
"7084","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari informed us about Marwa, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, Abdullah bin Kaysan told us, Ikrimah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, and Omar were pleased By God, on their authority, they came to the house of Abu Ayyub, and when they had eaten and were satisfied, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bread, meat, dates, fresh dates, and dates. “If you encounter something like this and strike it with your hands, then eat in the name of God and with God’s blessing.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7084 - True"
"7085","Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Amr Al-Saskiski, Abdullah Ibn Busr narrated to us, he said: My father said to my mother: If I prepared food for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she prepared Porridge was being reduced, so my father went and called him, and he placed his hand on it and then said: “Eat in the name of God.” So they took something similar to it, and when they ate it, he called for them and said: “O God, forgive them, have mercy on them, bless them, and provide for them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7085 - True"
"7086","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Qurra Al-Kindi, on the authority of Suleiman, may God be pleased with him, who said: I prepared food and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting, and I placed it in his hands. He said: “What is this?” I said: A gift, so he put his hand down and said to his companions: “Eat in the name of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7086 - True"
"7087","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Al-Hamdani told us, Affan told us, Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Badeel bin Maysara, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Umm Kulthum, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he eats If one of you eats food, let him say “In the Name of God,” and if he forgets at the beginning of it, let him say “In the Name of God” at its beginning and its end.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7087 - True"
"7088","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hudhayfah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he was brought food, and it came back. A Bedouin man came as if he was being expelled, so he took the hand, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his hand. Then a female slave came, and it was as if she was being expelled, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it. He greeted her by the hand and then said: “When Satan made you tired, the Bedouin and the slave girl came to make food permissible for them if the name of God was not mentioned over it.” In the name of God, eat.” Al-Hakim said: “This Abu Hudhayfah, whose name is Salama bin Suhayb, and he narrated on the authority of Aisha,” and the hadith is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7088 - True"
"7089","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Jabir bin In the morning, Al-Muthanna bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Khuza’i spoke to me, and I accompanied him to Wasit, where he used to say the name of God at the beginning and end of his food, so I asked him: I saw Your saying at the last morsel: In the name of God, at its beginning and at its end. He said: I tell you about that, that my grandfather Umayyah bin Makhshi, and he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him. I heard him say: A man was eating while the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was looking, and he did not say the name of God until it was at the end of his food, and he said: In the name of God, its beginning and its end. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Satan continued eating with him until he poisoned, and nothing remained in his stomach except “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7089 - True"
"7090","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, with Marwa, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad told us, Abd told us Al-Malik Ibn Abi Nadhrah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that a Jewish woman presented a sheep to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. When the people extended their hands, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: “Restrain your hands, for one of its members is telling me... It is poisoned.” He said: So he sent to its owner and said: “Has this food of yours been poisoned?” She said: Yes, I would love, if you were a liar, to relieve the people of you, and if you were truthful, I would know that God would inform you of it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Mention the name of God and eat.” So we ate, and none of us was harmed. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7090 - True"
"7091","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Ibn Abi told us Zaida, told us by Abu Ayyub Al-Afriqi, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Jariyah bint Wahb Al-Khuza’i, Hafsa narrated to me, May God be pleased with her, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to use his right hand for his food, drink, and clothing, and his left hand for everything else.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7091 - Its chain of transmission is unknown"
"7092","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah and Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, they said: Affan told us Ibn Muslim, Hammad Ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “When we We ate food with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We will not begin until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, begins. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7092 - True"
"7093","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Ramli told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hamza bin Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among some of his companions when Othman, may God be pleased with him, came leading a camel that had two burrs on it and was tied to its camel’s reins. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “What’s the matter with you?” He said: Flour, ghee, and honey. He said: “Bring it out.” So he plopped it, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for a large tumbler and put into it some of that flour and ghee. And honey, then he cooked it and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate and they ate and then he said to them: “Eat, for this is like the khabes of the people of Persia.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7093 - True"
"7094","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Sulaym al-Makki told us, Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabrah, on the authority of his father, he said: I was a delegate from Banu al-Muftafiq to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we did not meet him in his house. We did meet Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and she ordered a free woman for us. So it was made for us and we were brought with a mask - and the mask was a plate containing dates - then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “Have you achieved something or should I command you?” With something? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Then the shepherd raised his sheep to the resting places, and he had a saddle with him, leaving, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “What did you give birth to, O so-and-so?” He said: eagerly. He said: “Then slaughter for us a sheep in its place.” Then he turned to us and said: “Do not think. He did not say, ‘Do not think. We slaughtered it for your sake.’” One hundred sheep, and we do not want it to be more. If the shepherd gives birth to a lamb, we slaughter a sheep in its place. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have a wife. So he mentioned who Her long tongue and obscenity. He said: “Divorce her,” and I said: I have a son from her. He said: “Then command her - he says, advise her - and if there is good in her, she will do it, and do not strike your female slave the way you strike your female slave.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God. Tell me about ablution. He said: “Perform ablution thoroughly, interlace your fingers, and exhale the nose unless you are fasting.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7094 - True"
"7095","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abu Hilal Muhammad bin Sulaym told us, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: We made pottery for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I brought it to him and he looked at it. He scooped it up and said: “I thought it was meat.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, if Ishaq bin Abi Talha heard it from Jabir and they did not narrate it, and it contains A clear statement of the Messenger of God’s love for meat. And he witnessed it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7095 - True"
"7096","It was not narrated to me by Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balwayh. Ishaq bin Al-Hassan bin Maimun and Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us: Affan bin Muslim told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: - When my father was killed, he left a debt on me, and he mentioned the hadith in its length and mentioned it - I said to my wife: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He will come to us today at midday, so do not harm the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and do not speak to him. He said: So he came in and I made a bed and a pillow for him and he lay down. He shook his head and fell asleep, so I said to my master: Slay this she-camel while she is a fat domestic fowl, and the animal and the calf are empty before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wakes up. May God bless him and grant him peace, and I am with you. We did not stay there until we finished while he was sleeping. I said to him: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wakes up, he will pray By purification, and I fear that when he finishes getting up, he will not finish his ablution until we place the necklace in his hands. When he gets up, he said: “O Jabir, bring me “With purity.” He did not finish purifying himself until I placed the hug in his hands, and he looked at me and said: “It is as if you had made meat with meat. Call Abu Bakr for me.” Then he called his disciples who were with him and they entered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck his hand and said: “In the name of God, eat.” So they ate until they were satisfied and had enough. Among them is a lot of meat.” He mentioned the rest of the hadith. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7096 - True"
"7097","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of A man from Banu Fahm whose name I see is Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The best meat is the back meat.” It was narrated by Ruqabah bin Masqala on the authority of this scholar, but he did not attribute it to him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7097 - True"
"7098","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Sakouni told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami, and Al-Hussein bin Musab Al-Nakhi told us, They said: Yahya bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Raqbah bin Masqala, on the authority of a man, from Bani Fahm, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, May God be pleased with them. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best meat is the meat of the back.” The report has been authenticated with two chains of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7099","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Abu Abdul Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib Al-Nasa’i, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, They said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, my father told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Forbidden. He said: My father ordered me to take a harira and I did. Then he ordered me to carry it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was in his house and he said: “What is this, Jabir? Is this meat?” I said: No, O Messenger of God, but she is a silk woman that my father ordered me to do, so I did. Then he ordered me, so I carried her to you, then I returned to my father, and he said: Have you seen? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes. He said: What did he tell you? I said: He said: “Is this meat, Jabir?” My father said: Perhaps the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, craved meat, so he went to a domesticated animal of his, slaughtered it, roasted it, then ordered me to carry it. To him, and he said: I carried it to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God reward the Ansar well on our behalf, especially Abdullah bin Amr bin “It is forbidden and Sa’d bin Ubadah” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7099 - True"
"7100","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas said: I heard Anas say: I sent a rabbit to Al-Baqi’ and it became strong in its wake, so I was among those who became strong. So I raced them to it and took it and brought it to Abu Talha, so he ordered it to be slaughtered and then roasted, so its rump became incomplete and he sent it with me. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is this?” I said: The calf of a rabbit. Abu Talha sent it to you, and he accepted it from me. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7100 - True"
"7101","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, Saeed bin Abi Hilal told me, that Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah told him, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: “I was grilling “For the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the belly of the sheep, so he eats from it and then goes out to pray.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7101 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7102","Abu Abbas told us about Fawaid Ibn Abd al-Hakam. Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Ibn al-Hakam informed me. My father told me, and Shuaib Ibn Al-Layth, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, Khalid bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Rafi’, that Abu Ghatafan Al-Marri, told him on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: “I was grilling the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had performed ablution for prayer and he would eat from it.” Then he goes out to pray.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"7103","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, Abd al-Rahman bin Muawiya told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, he said: The Messenger of God saw me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I was taking the meat from the bone in my hand. He said to me: “O Safwan.” I said: At your service. He said: “Bring the meat close to you, for it is tastier and more satisfying.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7103 - True"
"7104","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Hasan told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Ibn al-Mubarak told us, Muammar informed us, On the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Do not eat the slice. It is the sacrifice of Satan.” Ibn al-Mubarak said: “The condition is that the spirit be expelled from him on the condition that the throat is not cut.” This hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7104 - True"
"7105","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us about fish, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Indeed, the devils inspire their guardians and say: ‘What has been sacrificed to God, do not eat it, and do not You slaughtered it, so eat it.” Then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: “And do not eat of that over which the name of God has not been mentioned” [Al-An’am: 121] “This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7105 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7106","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Hibban bin Hilal told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, so I met Zayd ibn Aslam, and he told me on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. A man whose camel wanted to die, so he slaughtered her with a stake, so I said to him: Iron? He said: No, but wood. So he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to eat it. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and the chain of narration is correct. On the condition of the two sheikhs, but I did not judge their condition to be correct because Malik bin Anas, may God have mercy on him, sent it in Al-Muwatta on the authority of Zaid bin “He converted to Islam”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7106 - Sahih Gharib"
"7107","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed me, Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed me, Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us, Shu`bah informed me, and he said: Abd informed me. Allah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Hadir bin Muhajir al-Bahili, saying: I heard Suleiman bin Yassar narrated on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit: “A wolf bitten a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a hammer, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission to eat it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7107 - True"
"7108","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, and Al-Hasan bin Al-Mufaddal told us, and Ismail bin Ali Al-Khatbi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi and Muhammad bin Ghalib said: Al-Hasan bin Bishr bin Salem told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.” A trustworthy follower of him was Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad. The Meccan cup"
"7109","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ubayy, Muhammad bin Nu’aym, and Ahmad bin Salamah told us, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Attab bin Bashir told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ziyad Al-Qaddah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.” Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, we told him. Muhammad bin Yahya, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanathili told me, and he mentioned it: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” It is only known from the hadith of Ibn Abi Laila and Hammad bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, and it was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Abu Hurairah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7109 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7110","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Al-Hasan bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, my father told me, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slaughter of the fetus his mother's slaughter"
"7111","Abu Al-Walid told us, Al-Hussein bin Sufyan told us, Wahb bin Baqiya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hassan Al-Wasiti told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The slaughter of a fetus, when it feels, is the slaughter of its mother.” But it must be slaughtered until all the blood in it is drained.” This is a large chapter that deals with the paths of Atiyya on the authority of Abu Sa’id. For this reason, they did not narrate it, and perhaps “He is under the delusional illusion that the hadith of Abu Ayyub is authentic, but it is not so.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7111 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7112","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq and Ahmad bin Ja’far bin Nasr Al-Razi told us, in others who said: Yusuf bin Musa, Abdullah bin Al-Jahm Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ala’ bin Shaybah told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Laila, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ibn Abu Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The killing of the fetus is the killing of its mother.” And the hadith of Abu Al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, ‘Allan was the only one to mention it, and it includes Ziyad, and he has many mistakes for which there is no evidence. And whoever ponders this topic among the people of “It was decided in ‘Ajab’ that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not record it in the two Sahih books.”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7112 - It is not correct"
"7113","Ali bin Muhammad bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Muhammad bin Sharik told us. Al-Makki, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’a’a, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The people of pre-Islamic times used to eat And they leave things filthy, so God Almighty sent His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sent down His Book and made lawful what He had lawful and forbidden what He had forbidden. He made lawful, then it is lawful, and whatever he forbade is forbidden, and whatever he remained silent about is pardoning.” And he recited this verse: “Say, ‘I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden to me. Ta’im} [Al-An’am: 145] The verse: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7113 - True"
"7114","Ali bin Issa told me, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Hurashi told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Makhoul, On the authority of Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has set limits, so do not transgress them, and He has imposed for you Obligations, so do not neglect them, and he has forbidden things, so do not violate them, and he left out things without forgetfulness from your Lord, but as a mercy from Him to you, so accept them. And do not search in it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7114 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7115","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati narrated to us, Munjab bin Al-Harith narrated to us, Saif bin Harun Al-Burjami narrated to us, On the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about ghee and cheese. And Al-Farra said: “Permissible is what God has made lawful in His Book, and what is forbidden is what God has forbidden in His Book, and whatever He is silent about is among what He has pardoned.” This hadith. It is authentic and interpreted in the chapter, but Saif bin Harun did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7115 - A sword they did not bring out"
"7116","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulayman Al-Wasiti told us, Abbad told us Ibn Al-Awwam, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to like dregs,” so I heard Abu Muhammad saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq say: “Domace is porridge.”"
"7117","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Al-Hadrami Muhammad bin Shuja’ told us, Al-Mubarak bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The most beloved food to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was porridge.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, for this Omar bin Saeed is the brother of Sufyan and Al-Mubarak is the son of Saeed. As for his saying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over all other foods.” It is mentioned in the two Sahihs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7117 - True"
"7118","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib said: We were invited to a meal, and then Sa’id bin Jubayr, then Maqsim, then so-and-so, then so-and-so, and Sa’id bin Jubayr said to them: When Put down the lid: Have any of you heard what is said about food? Miqsam said: Talk to them. He said: Ibn Abbas narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its edges and do not eat.” From his midst: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7118 - True"
"7119","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Yunus Al-Tanisi told us, Khalid bin Yazid bin Abu Malik, on the authority of his father, that he told him on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, and he was one of the people of Al-Safa. He said: We stayed for three days and he was among the people of Al-Safa. He goes out to the mosque, takes the two and three men by the hand as much as he can, and feeds them. He said: I was among those who missed him for three days. And its nights. He said: So I saw Abu Bakr at nightfall, so I went to him and recited to him from Surat Saba, so he reached his house and I hoped that they would invite me. To the food, he recited to me until he reached the door of the house, then he stood at the door until he read to me the rest, then he entered and left me, and then I was exposed to Omar. So I did the same to him, and he mentioned that he did the same as what Abu Bakr had done. So when I woke up, I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him, and he said to the maid: “Is there anything?” She said: Yes, a loaf and a lump of ghee. So he called for it, then crumbled the bread in his hand, then took that lump of ghee and rolled that bread. Then he gathered it in his hand until he made it into porridge, then he said: “Go, call for me ten, of whom you are the companion.” So I called ten, of whom I am the companion, and then he said: “Sit down,” and I placed the bowl down, then he said: “Eat in the name of God. Eat from its sides and do not eat from the top, for the blessing descends from Then we ate until we were at the top, as if we had traced it with our fingers. Then he took some of it, fixed some of it, and returned it. Then he said: “Pray for me.” “Ten” and he mentioned that after that he called “ten” twice and said: “They have preferred something.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7119 - Khaled was considered trustworthy by some of them, and Al-Nasa’i said he is not trustworthy"
"7120","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Kaab bin Malik, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that “he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he ate food, he licked his three fingers.” with which he ate”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7120 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7121","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ka’b Ibn Malik, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “When he ate, he licked his three fingers.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7121 - True"
"7122","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ulayya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sa'ib bin Barakat Al-Makki, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took His family was ill. He ordered soup, and it was made. Then he would order it and they would drink some of it, and he would say: “It is more than enough for the heart of the sick person - or less than Fouad Al-Saqeem - “Just as one of you wipes the dirt from her face with water” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7122 - True"
"7123","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Ahmad bin Hafs told me, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, about Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Muhajireen and Ansar digging a trench around Medina. And they move the dirt on their backs, saying:
 [The sea of rage]

 We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad... on Islam as long as we remain.
 The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, answers them and says: “Oh God, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so bless the Ansar and the Muhajirs.” Then he came. With a plate containing a handful of crushed barley that had been made with great care, so it was placed in the hands of the people while they were hungry, and it had a sore throat on the throat. And it has a scent: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this addition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7123 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7124","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Qurra bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them, that when she became angry, she would cover him until he went away immediately. And you say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, it is greater in blessing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim in the evidence, and it was not They narrate it, “and it has an interpreter’s witness from the hadith of Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Azrami.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7124 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7125","We were told by Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim, the Bukhari jurist in Nisapur, Salih bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Al-Azrami, my father told me, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cool hot food, for Spicy food without blessing.”"
"7126","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told me, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “None of you should wipe his hand with a handkerchief until he licks His hand, for a man does not know which of his food will be blessed for him, and Satan is lurking for people - or man - in everything, even when eating his food.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7126 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7127","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Mawardi told us, Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Yaqoub bin Al-Walid, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id Al-Maqbari, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The devil is a sensitive toucher, so beware of him for yourselves. Whoever sleeps with a wind in his hand and something befalls him, then nothing happens.” “He blames no one but himself.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with these words.
 ["
"7128","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Kufi, the one-eyed Mullah, said that he heard Anas bin Malik say: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stand behind him and put his food in “The land, and he responds to the call of the slave, and rides the donkey.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7128 - Muslim Turk"
"7129","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Uqba bin Khaled Al-Sakouni narrated to me, in Kufa. My father narrated to me, on the authority of his father Al-Hasan bin Uqba, on the authority of his father, Uqba bin Khaled Al-Sakouni, on the authority of Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you eat, take off your shoes, for it will remove your body.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7129 - I think it is fabricated and its chain of transmission is dark"
"7130","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, dictating, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Asbahani told us, narrated to us Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri, Omar bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from two prayers, two recitations, two foods, and two clothes. He forbade me from praying after the morning prayer until the sun rose and after the afternoon prayer until the sun set, and from eating while lying on my stomach. “I wear a blind garment and hide myself in one garment, so that there is no covering between my private parts and the sky.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7130 - Omar Wah"
"7131",""
"7132","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani informed me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told me, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi informed me, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I was in Suffah and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to us some Ajwa dates.” So he poured for us, and we were joining the two together out of hunger. When one of us joined, he said to his companions: “I have joined the two together.” So they joined. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7132 - True"
"7133","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Amr Al-Muzani, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The stick and the rock “From Paradise.” This is what we told him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7133 - True"
"7134","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh informed us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdullah told us Al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Mish’al bin Iyas told us, Amr bin Sulaym told me, he said: I heard Rafi’ bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The stick and the rock are from Paradise.” This is how we told him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7134 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7135","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdullah told us Al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Mish’al bin Iyas told us, Amr bin Sulaym told me, he said: I heard Rafi’ bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The stick and the rock are from Paradise.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, for this Mish’al is Amr. Ibn Iyas is a sheikh from the people of Basra who speaks little of the hadith.”"
"7136","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Azraq told us, Mahdi bin Maymun told us, On the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to eat fresh dates and throw stones on his head.” Al-Qana’: Al-Tabaq “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7136 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7137","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Sulaiman bin Harb, and Amr bin Marzuq told us, they said: Yusuf bin Attiyah, Matar al-Warraq told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take The fresh dates in his right hand and the watermelon in his left, so he ate the fresh dates with the watermelon, and it was the most beloved fruit to him.” This is a hadith that was unique to Yusuf ibn Atiyya, and they did not use it as evidence. Rather, this text is known with a word other than this, from the hadith of Aisha, may God be pleased with her.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7137 - It was unique to Yusuf"
"7138","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad Al-Taymi told us, and Abu Al-Rabi’ Suleiman bin Daoud Al-Ataki told us, And Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami, they said, Abu Zukair told us Yahya bin Muhammad bin Qais, he said: I heard Hisham bin Urwa mentioning on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat dates with dates, for when Satan eats them, the son of Adam He became angry and said, “The son of Adam remains until he eats the new creation.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7138 - An objectionable hadith"
"7139","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: And he told me Muawiyah bin Salih said: I heard Yahya bin Jabir, narrating on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him, he said: “The son of Adam does not carry any vessel worse than the stomach of a Muslim. A Muslim is considered to be food that will strengthen his backbone. If there is no inevitable situation, then a third is for his food and a third for his drink and a third for himself.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7139 - True"
"7140","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Rabi’ah Fahd bin Awf told us, Fadl bin Abi Al-Fadl told us. Al-Azdi, Omar bin Musa told me, Ali bin Al-Aqmar told me, on the authority of Abu Juhayfa, he said: I ate porridge made of whole wheat bread and fatty meat, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I started burping. He said: “This is not enough of your belching, for the most satisfied people in this world are the ones who are most satisfied.” “The afterlife through hunger.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7140 - Fahd bin Awf said that Al-Madani is a liar and Omar is a perisher."
"7141","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Israel, saying: I heard Ja`dah, saying: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: And he saw a man who was full, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gestured. With his hand to his stomach and saying: “If this had been other than this, it would have been better for him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7141 - True"
"7142","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Apply oil and anoint yourself with it, for it is from a tree “Blessed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7142 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7143","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Abdul-Quddus bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Kabir told us Bin Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, Muhammad bin Abdul-Kabir narrated to me, my uncle Abdul-Salam bin Shuaib narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a cup containing milk and some honey, and he said: “A cup of honey is in a vessel. I do not eat it, nor do I prohibit it.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7143 - Rather, it is reprehensible and false"
"7144","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Hani Al-Khawlani told me, On the authority of Abu Ali al-Juhani, who is Amr ibn Malik, on the authority of Fadalah ibn Ubaid, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The most successful is he who is guided to Islam and whose livelihood is sufficient and who is content with it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7144 - True"
"7145","Abu Yahya Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Samarqandi told me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Nasr told us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzouq Al-Bahili, Bishr bin Al-Mubarak Al-Rasibi told us, he said: I went with my grandfather to a banquet in which the Qattan was predominant. He said: Then the brothers were brought. Then the people took hold of their hands, and I heard the foreman say: What is the matter with them that they do not eat? They said: They are waiting for Adam. Ghalib said: Karima bint Hammam Al-Ta’iyya told us, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Honor bread, and the dignity of bread is that one does not wait for it.” So he ate it and we ate. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7145 - True"
"7146","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Attar told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Marudhi told us, Suleiman bin Qurum, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: I and a friend of mine entered Salman’s, may God be pleased with him, and he brought bread and salt to us and said: “If it had not been for The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from being extravagant, I would be extravagant for you.” My companion said: “If there was sa’atar in our salt, then he would send it to purify it.” To the grocer, he pawned it. He brought a piece of food and threw it in it. When we ate, my friend said: Praise be to God, who satisfied us with what He provided us with. Salman said: If only I was content with what I was provided with. My purification was not pledged to the grocer. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He did not narrate it and he has a witness similar to this.” Attribution
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7146 - True"
"7147","Ali bin Abdullah told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Rammas told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Masoud told us. Al-Abdi said: I heard Salman Al-Farisi, may God be pleased with him, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from acting in front of a guest.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7147 - Its chain of transmission is soft"
"7148","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, about Ubayd Allah ibn Zuhar, on the authority of Ali ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The I am most envied by people because of a believer who has little discernment and has limited ability to pray, who worships God well and obeys Him in secret, and who is obscure to the people and not referred to. with the fingers, and his provision was sufficient, so he was patient in that.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shook it with his finger and said: “His death has hastened.” Its fruits are few and its heritage is few. This is an authentic chain of narration for the Levantines according to them, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7148 - To weakness is"
"7149","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed told us Bin Abi Ayyub, Shurahbil bin Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Successful is he who embraces Islam and is provided with an adequate provision, and whom God is content with what He has given him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7149 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7150","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdullah bin Ja`far told us, Zaid told us Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, he said: In pre-Islamic times, people used to collect humpstones. camels and cut off the buttocks of the sheep and eat them and carry the carcasses of them. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, they asked him about that. He said: “Whatever animal is cut while it is alive is dead.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out. “It was said on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, On the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7150 - True"
"7151","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Yahya bin Hassan told us, Miswar bin Al-Salt told us, and Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about Asnama’s graves. Camels and the goats of sheep, and he said: “Whatever is cut from a living animal is dead.” Narrated by Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Bilal, on the authority of Zaid. Ibn Aslam “messenger”, and it was said on the authority of Zayd Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Umar"
"7152","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, Musa bin Harun Al-Bardi told us, Maan told us Bin Musa, Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What was cut off of an animal while it is alive is dead.”"
"7153","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Abu Usama told us, Hammad ibn Al-Sa'ib, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “All musk is tanned.” So I said to him: “We are traveling with these foreigners, and they have pots in which they cook carcasses and the flesh of pigs.” He said: “What? “If it is of pottery, boil water in it, then wash it. And if it is of copper, wash it, for water is a purification of everything.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7153 - True"
"7154","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Harmala bin Abdul Aziz bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra Al-Juhani, Abu Abdul Aziz bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace to his companions when the stone came down: “Whoever makes food from this water, let him throw it in.” He said: “And among them are those who knead the dough, and among them are those who “He felt the hair, so they threw it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7154 - And on one of the two conditions"
"7155","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib and Ishaq bin Al-Hassan told us, they said: Affan told us, Abu Awanah, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra, may God be pleased with him, who said: A mule died with a man, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He asked him to ask him for a fatwa, and Jabir claimed on the authority of Samurah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to its owner: “Do you not have anything that will suffice for it?” He said: No. He said: “Go and eat it all.” It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7155 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7156","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, in Marwa, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Hassan bin Atiya told us, on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are in a fertile land, so what is permissible for us of dead animals? He said: “If you do not wake up in the morning and you do not go to sleep and do not celebrate it, then it is your business.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7156 - There is an interruption"
"7157","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, dictating, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, and Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Saleh Al-Samarqandi, Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Kharijah reported, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, On the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you see your family with cloudy milk, avoid what he forbade.” “May God protect him from a dead person.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it and it has a basis with a correct chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7157 - True"
"7158","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, my father told us, on the authority of his father, Ibn Aoun told us, he said: I read with Al-Hasan the letter of Samurah. Ibn Jundub, to his sons, in which it says that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “From what is necessary - or necessary - sunrise or sunshine is sufficient.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7158 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7159","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Al-Haytham bin Kharijah told us, Al-Mu’afia bin Imran told us, On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, on the authority of Umm Abdullah, sister of Shaddad bin Aws, that she was sent To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a cup of milk when he broke his fast, and that was during the long day and the intense heat. The Messenger replied to her: How can you do this? Yogurt? She said: From a sheep of mine. He said: Where did you get this sheep? She said: I bought it with my own money, so he drank. The next day, the mother of Abdullah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: O Messenger of God. I sent you that milk as a pity for you because of the extreme heat and the long day, so I returned it to me along with the Messenger, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “With that “The Messengers were commanded: ‘Do not eat anything but what is good and do what is right.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7159 - Ibn Abi Maryam is weak"
"7160","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, Zaid bin Aslam told me, On the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you enters upon his brother So he feeds him food, let him eat from it and does not ask him about it, and if he gives him something to drink, let him drink from it and does not ask him about it.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and he did not narrate it, and it has a valid witness according to the condition of Muslim alone.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7160 - True"
"7161","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, May God be pleased with him, according to a narration that he said: “If you go to your Muslim brother and he feeds you food, then eat and do not ask him, and if he gives you something to drink, drink it and do not ""You ask him""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7161 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7162","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Zur’ah told us Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi, Sa`id bin Bashir told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God protect you from the rulers of They will be after me.” He said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “Whoever enters upon them and speaks truthfully to them and helps them in their oppression is not of me and will not come to me at the Basin.”
 “Know, O Abdul Rahman, that fasting is a shield and prayer is proof.”
 “O Abdul-Rahman, God has refused to allow me to admit to Paradise flesh that grew from unclean things, so Hell is more deserving of it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7162 - True"
"7163","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God protect you, O Ka’b Ibn Ujrah is from the leadership of the fools. He said: What is the leadership of the fools? He said: “There will be princes after me who do not follow my guidance and do not follow my Sunnah. So whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their injustice?” Those are not of me, and I am not of them, and they do not belong to my coffin, and whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their injustice, then those are of me. And I am one of them, and they will attack my basin. O Ka’b bin Ujrah, no meat that grew from unlawful things will enter Paradise. Hell is more deserving of it. O Ka’b bin Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is an offering - or he said: proof - “His saying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was narrated.” And he said: “Flesh that grew from filth, on the authority of Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7163 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7164","So Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Qurrah bin Habib told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Aslam. Al-Kufi, on the authority of Murrah Al-Tayeb, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever’s flesh grows from unlawful things, hellfire.” more deserving of it”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7164 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7165","Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary, so Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastawayh told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Yazid bin Abdul Malik reported, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Who “His flesh grew from evil and into the fire.”"
"7166","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Sahl Al-Mujawiz told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Suleiman bin Musa said: Waqqas ibn Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Al-Mustarid ibn Shaddad, my brother of Banu Fahm, he told him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever eats A Muslim will be given a meal with which God will feed him a meal from the fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever places a Muslim in a position of reputation, God will raise him up on the Day of Resurrection. The Resurrection is a place of reputation and hypocrisy, and whoever covers a Muslim with a garment, God will clothe him with a garment from the fire of the Day of Resurrection. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7166 - True"
"7167","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Al-Layth told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he used to say On the pulpit: “I protect the wealth of the weak, the orphan and the woman.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7167 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7168","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Hazim told us, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar Al-Aslami, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority, she says: Umm Sunbulah gave milk to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she came to me with it, but she did not find it, so I said to her: Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He forbade us from eating the food of the Bedouins, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr entered and said: “O Umm Sunbula, what Is this with you? She said: O Messenger of God, milk I gave you as a gift. He said: “Pour it, O Umm Sunbula.” So he gave it to Abu Bakr, then he said: “Pour it, O Umm Sunbula.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it and drank. She said: So I said: Oh, how cold it is on the liver. Aisha said: O Messenger of God, you told us that you forbade the food of the Bedouins. He said: “O Aish, they are not Bedouins. They are the people of our desert and we are the people of their metropolis. And when they are called and they respond, they are not Bedouins.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7168 - True"
"7169","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, may God Almighty have mercy on him, Hussam bin Al-Siddiq narrated to us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywa bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Salim bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Qais Al-Tajibi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Do not keep company with anyone except a believer, and let no one eat your food except a pious person.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7169 - True"
"7170","Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahmi told me, my father told me, on the authority of Harun bin Musa Al-Nahwi, On the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade food “The two contending that it should be eaten” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7170 - True"
"7171","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Kathir bin Hisham told us, Ja’far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade two foods: sitting at a table.” He drinks alcohol over it, or the man eats while lying on his stomach. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7171 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7172","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Munqidh Al-Khawlani told us, in Egypt, Idris bin Yahya Al-Khawlani told us, Raja bin Abi Ata told me, on the authority of Wahib bin Abdullah Al-Kaabi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever feeds his brother bread until he is satisfied and gives him water to drink until he quenches his thirst, God will keep him away from the Fire by seven ditches.” “After the distance between two ditches is a journey of five hundred years.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7172 - True"
"7173","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hanafi told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abu Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The expiations are feeding food “And spreading the greetings of peace and prayer at night while the people are asleep.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7173 - Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Humaid said that Ahmad abandoned his hadith."
"7174","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam bin Yahya told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Abu Maimuna, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, inform me of a matter when you take it. Did you enter heaven? He said: “Spread peace, provide food, maintain ties with relatives, and spend the night while the people are asleep, and enter Paradise in peace.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7174 - True"
"7175","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub informed us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, Abu Al-Samh narrated to him that Abu Al-Haytham narrated to him on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Any man who earns money from what is lawful and feeds and clothes himself, then from among God’s creation, there is zakat for him.”
 “Any Muslim man who does not have charity, let him say in his supplication, O God, bless Muhammad, your servant and messenger, and bless the believing men and women. And the Muslim men, male and female, for it is zakat.”
 And he said: “No believer who listens to good is satisfied until his final destination is Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7175 - True"
"7176","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim, Fadl bin Marzuq told us, Adi bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, I am overcome with distress. So he sent for his wives, but he did not find anything with them. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he greeted: “Is there a man who is hosting tonight, may God have mercy on him?” Then a man from the Ansar stood up and said: “I am, O Messenger of God.” So he went to his family and said: To his wife: The guest of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we will not spare any of it. She said: By God, I only have food for the girl. He said: If he wants The boys had dinner, so put them to sleep, and come, turn off the lamp, and let us cover our bellies for the night. So she did, and then the man went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has marveled - that is, God Almighty has laughed at so-and-so and so-and-so.” And God Almighty sent down {And they give preference to themselves, even if they are in poverty} [Al-Hashr: 9] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7176 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7177","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Muhammad bin Fada’ told me, my father told me, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you buys meat, add more broth to it. If one of you does not drink meat, he should drink broth, which is one of the two meats.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7177 - Muhammad bin Fazza’ Al-Azdi was deemed weak by Ibn Ma’in"
"7178","Abdan bin Zayd bin Yaqoub Al-Daqqaq told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas Al-Asqalani told us, Shayban bin Abdul Rahman told us, Abdul Malik bin Umair told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out at an hour when he does not go out and no one meets him, so Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, came to him and said: “What brings you, Abu Bakr?” He said: I went out to meet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to look at his face and to greet him, and it was not long before Omar came, may God be pleased with him, and he said To him: “What brings you, O Omar?” He said: Hunger, O Messenger of God. He said: “And I found some of that.” So they went to the house of Abu Al-Haytham bin Al-Tayhan Al-Ansari, who was a man who had a lot of palm trees and arable trees. And there was none of the servants, and they did not find him. They said to his wife, “Where is your friend?” She said: Go and fetch water for us.It was not long before Abu al-Haytham brought a waterskin, which he disturbed and put down. Then he came and committed himself to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and ransoms him. With his father and mother, he went with them to a garden and spread out a rug for them, then he went to a palm tree and brought a qanoo and placed it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Did you not select for us a wetland?” He said: O Messenger of God, I wanted you to choose from fresh and fresh water, so they ate and drank from that water. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “By God, this is the bliss for which you will be held accountable on the Day of Resurrection: cool shade, fresh, fresh water, and cool water.” So Abu set off. Al-Haytham went to prepare food for them, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Do not slaughter a young female.” So he slaughtered for them a male goat or a young kid, and he brought it to them. So they ate, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you have a servant?” He said: No, he said: If a captive came to me, then he came to us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with two heads, without a third, so Abu Al-Haytham came to him. He said: O Messenger of God, a servant. So he said to him: “Choose from them.” He said: O Messenger of God, choose for me.Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The advisor is trustworthy. Take this, for I saw him praying and enjoined him with kindness.” So Abu al-Haytham set off. The servant went to his wife and told her what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had said. Then his wife said to him: You are not aware of what he said about it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, unless you free him. He said: He is freed. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty has not sent a prophet or a caliph except that he has two inner circles, a female inner circle who commands him to do good.” And forbid him from evil, and with a hidden secret that you do not miss. He who protects himself from the hidden evil has been protected. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Yunus bin Ubaid and Abdullah bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. It is more complete and longer than the hadith This is Abu Hurairah
 It was narrated by Bakkar Al-Sirini, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar Al-Amri, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in an hour He was not going out there, and Abu Bakr came out and said: “What brought you out, Abu Bakr?” He said: Hunger - the hadith was narrated by him
 Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, on the authority of his uncle Abu al-Ahwas,He said: Abdullah said: “We used to count the candles in pre-Islamic times. A man is invited to eat, and someone else takes with him. He was not invited, and today he is among you.” “The one whose religion is correct is the men.” Sahih “narrated by
 Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, “This is also true.”
 He narrated it
 Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abu Talha, who is Nu`aym bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Any guest He stayed with a people and the guest became deprived. He has the right to take as much as his village, and there is no blame on him.” Sahih. “As for the hadith of Yunus bin Ubaid.”
 [p. 147]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7178 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim
 [p. 146]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7178 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7179","So Ammar bin Abdul-Jabbar informed me, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Al-Judi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Abi Karimah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whenever a Muslim hosts a people and the guest becomes deprived, it is the duty of every Muslim to support him until he takes a village.” his night of his crops and wealth.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7179 - True"
"7180","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If you come upon a shepherd, call him three times. He will answer you. Otherwise, drink without spoiling. And when you come to the wall of a garden, call the owner of the garden three times. If he answers you, otherwise... “Eat without spoiling.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7180 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7181","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father Ishaq bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his uncle Ishaq bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Yazid, on the authority of Umair, The master of Abi al-Lahm, and Umair was a master of the Banu Ghifarah. He said: I came with my masters, intending to emigrate, until we approached the city. They left me in They appeared and entered the city, and a severe famine struck me. Some of the people of the city who passed by me said to me: If you enter some of the walls of I went to Medina and took some of its dates. I entered a wall and came to a palm tree and cut two stalks from it. Then, behold, the owner of the wall took me out until a messenger came. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He asked me about my situation, so I told him. He said: “Which of the two is better?” So I pointed to one of them, and he ordered me to take it, and he ordered the owner of the wall to take the other one, and he let me go. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7181 - True"
"7182","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Abbad bin Shurahbil, he said: A famine struck us, so I came to Medina and entered one of its walls, so I took An ear of corn, so I rubbed it, ate from it, and put some of it on my dress, then the owner of the wall came and hit me and took my dress, so I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “I did not teach him if he was ignorant, nor did I feed him if he was hungry or hungry.” He said: He returned the garment to me and ordered me half a wasq or one wasq. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7182 - True"
"7183","Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, and Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, saying: Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi informed us, Asim bin Suwayd told us, about Muhammad bin Musa bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the children of On Wednesday, Amr bin Awf saw something that he had not seen before from his fort on the palm trees, and he said: “If only you came This is your Eid. You stayed until you heard what I said. They said: Yes, through our fathers, O Messenger of God, and our mothers. He said: When they attended the Friday prayer, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the Friday prayer with them, then he prayed two rak’ahs in the mosque and was departing to his home. Before that day, then he turned and faced the people with his face, and the Ansar, or whoever was among them, followed him until he brought them to him. He said: “O community of Ansar.” They said: At your service, that is, the Messenger of God. He said: “In pre-Islamic times, when you did not worship God, you would bear all things. And you will do what is right with your property and you will do what you do to the wayfarer, until God has bestowed upon you Islam and has bestowed His Prophet upon you. You protect your wealth, and for whatever the son of Adam eats there is a reward, and for whatever the beast or bird eats there is a reward.” So the people returned, and there was not one of them except He demolished thirty gates from his garden. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it contains the clear prohibition of fortifying walls, palm trees, and other things.” Of the types of fruits for the needy and hungry to eat from.” The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, included the hadith of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them. On their authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When one of you enters his brother’s room, he should eat from him and not take food.”"
"7184","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me, in Mecca, Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Yazid bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Masmoul told us Al-Qasim bin Makhoul Al-Nahdi, he heard his father saying: I said: O Messenger of God, we meet camels with milk in them. It is destined and we are in need. He said: “Call to the owner of the camels three times, and if he comes, otherwise, milk, milk, and let, then express and let the milk remain.” ""For his reasons""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7184 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7185","Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, Yunus told us Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to the women, a woman came up to him Jalila, as if she were one of the women of Mudar, so she said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we are beholden to our fathers, our sons, and our wives, so what is lawful for us? Of their money? He said: “You can eat fresh dates and give them as gifts.” It was narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7185 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7186","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Habib told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: A woman said: O Messenger of God, we are burdened by our sons and brothers, so what? Is it permissible for us to use their wealth? He said: “The fresh food is what you eat and give as a gift.” The hadith of Abd al-Salam bin Harb is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"7187","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr Al-Bari told us, Ubi told us, Suwayd bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God God Almighty will admit three people into Paradise with a morsel of bread, a handful of dates, and similar things that benefit the needy: the one who commands it and the righteous wife. And the servant who brings food to the poor.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God who has not forgotten our servants.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7187 - Suwayd bin Abdul Aziz is abandoned"
"7188","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Al-Khalil told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat and drink and give in charity without extravagance or imagination.” “Indeed, God Almighty loves to see the effect of His grace on His servant.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7188 - True"
"7189","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bakr ibn Sawadah, that Sufyan ibn Wahb told him on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, that he sent to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with food of vegetables that contained onions or leeks, but he did not see any trace of it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, refused to eat it. He eats it and he said to him: What prevents you from eating it? He said: I did not see the impact of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am ashamed before the angels of God Almighty, and I am not “By Muharram.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7189 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7190","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Hakam narrated to us, narrated to us Shu’bah, Ali bin Zaid told me, he said: I heard Abu Al-Mutawakkil, speaking on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The king of India to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a jar containing ginger, so he fed his companions piece by piece, and he fed me with a piece of it,” Al-Hakim said. May God Almighty have mercy on him: “I did not extract a single letter from the beginning of this book to Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud’an al-Qurashi, may God Almighty have mercy on him.” “I did not remember anything other than ginger in the food of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I took it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7190 - This is what they weakened because of the age that Ahmad left behind"
"7191","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, Amer told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan said: I witnessed a feast in the house of Abdul-Ala, and with us was Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him. When we finished He got up and said: I do not want to be a preacher, but I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he finished eating, saying: “Praise be to God.” “Plenty, good and blessed, not to be deposited or to be dispensed with.” This is a hadith with a sound chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and the evidence of it is more correct and more famous. “narrators from it”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7191 - True"
"7192","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, Thawr told us, Khaled told us. Ibn Maadan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was removed from his hands, he would say: “Praise be to God, abundant, good and blessed praise be to Him, which cannot be neglected or dispensed with, our Lord.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7192 - True"
"7193","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Maysarah, On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: “We had a sheep and we feared it would die, so we killed it and divided it except its shoulder.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7193 - True"
"7194","Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Hayyan Al-Qadi told us, Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Saji told us, Bishr bin Hilal told us, Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami told us, he said: I heard Maan bin Muhammad, narrating on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, who said: Hanzalah and I were in Al-Baqi’ with Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with them. On his authority, Abu Hurairah told us, in Al-Baqi’, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “A grateful feeder is like a patient fasting person.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7194 - True"
"7195","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Ubayd Allah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Hurra, on the authority of Hakim bin Abi Hurra, on the authority of Salman Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I only know him. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, the one who feeds and is grateful has a reward equal to that of a patient fasting person.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7195 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7196","Azhar bin Hamdoun the caller told me, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Mufaddal bin Fadala, on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took A leper, so he put it with him in the bowl and then said: “In the name of God, trusting in God and trusting in Him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7196 - True"
"7197","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Hafs Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Madaini told us, Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “Whoever spends the night with an abyss in his hand and some calamity happens to him, let no one blame anyone but himself.” These chains of narrations are all authentic, and they did not narrate it."
"7198","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, my father told us, Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Ya’qub bin Al-Walid told us Al-Madani, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Satan is a sensitive toucher, so beware of him for yourselves. Whoever spends the night with a cloud in his hand and something befalls him, let him blame no one but himself.”"
"7199","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Husayn Al-Himyari, On the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khair, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever eats what he swallows with his tongue, let him swallow what Let him speak. Whoever does it has done well, and whoever does not, there is no blame. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It was not narrated by “The Last Book of Foods.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7199 - True"
